  "name": "Question 11",
  "problem": "Given the Cartesian equation $5x-7y+4z+20=0$ of the plane $\u03a0$, find an equation of $\u03a0$ in the form $(r-p)\\cdot n=0.$\n\n$(r-\u27e80,0,$\n{{field-1}}\n$\u27e9)\\cdot \u27e85,$\n{{field-2}}\n,\n{{field-3}}\n$\u27e9=0$",
  "worked_solution": "First, from the equation of the plane we get that the normal vector of $\u03a0$ is $n=\u27e85,-7,4\u27e9.$\n\nNow, we solve the Cartesian equation of $\u03a0$ for $z$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-7y+4z+20 & =0 \\\\ z & =-\\frac{5}{4}x+\\frac{7}{4}y-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we put $x=0$ and $y=0$, we get $z=-5.$ Hence, the point $P(0,0,-5)$ lies on $\u03a0.$ Note that the position vector of $P$ is $p=\u27e80,0,-5\u27e9.$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(r-p)\\cdot n & =0 \\\\ (r-\u27e80,0,-5\u27e9)\\cdot \u27e85,-7,4\u27e9 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
